Z||000000||billfredmike24||04-08-2001||04:25 PM||||Do you need a safety on your car in the U.S. before you put any insurance on it.  Does anyone know how much they cost if the car is in good shape and needs nothing to safety? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||04-08-2001||07:14 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by billfredmike24:<BR><B>Do you need a safety on your car in the U.S. before you put any insurance on it.  Does anyone know how much they cost if the car is in good shape and needs nothing to safety? </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I guess I dont understand what you mean by saftey..<P>Some states do require emissions testing in order for it to be certified, and then I believe you can get it registered with the state you are in, and after that you can get it insured.  I am not sure about that though, Michigan doesnt require any testing.  All I do here is go to the secretary of state, get it registered, and then call up the insurance company and then the send me the proff of insurance papers.  <P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||04-08-2001||09:38 PM||||Some states require safety checks. Some don't. <BR>In Georgia, they don't care if your car is shedding parts as it goes down the road, as long as the exhaust is clean, and the cat is still in place. If you don't live close to Atlanta (or Macon, I think), you don't even have to pass an emissions test. I believe the Northeastern states are a little tougher.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000003||billfredmike24||04-08-2001||10:55 PM||||In ontario before you can get insurance you have to have the car safetied.  Garage has to check the car out and gives you a safety to be sure everything is ok. Costs like $50 i think.||||reg||1
Z||000004||danny boy||04-08-2001||11:29 PM|||| Kinda like an inspection sticker.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||04-09-2001||12:18 AM||||All states have a "safety Check Law" It just that some states like to do them on a regular basis. The "safety" checks are usually checking to make sure all lights work and are DOT approved. Brakes work (regular and emergency) Tires have legal tread, safety features work (seatbelts, airbags on newer cars), No cracked glass, and the likes. Some states do it if you purchase a vehicle from outside the state and register it in that state.||||reg||1
